MOUNTPROBE(1)

NAME
    mountprobe - exercise SmallOS mount-table and statfs compatibility

SYNOPSIS
    mountprobe

DESCRIPTION
    mountprobe validates the kernel-backed mount table for the ext2 root
    filesystem, /proc, /dev, and dynamic proc/devtmpfs pseudo mounts. It checks
    /proc/mounts output, statfs and fstatfs filesystem identities,
    unsupported mount failures, and busy unmount failures.

    This probe intentionally documents the current mount milestone boundary:
    proc and devtmpfs can be mounted on existing ext2 directories, while
    arbitrary ext2 stacking and unsupported filesystem types are still gated.
